{
  "_note": "The block roster for Abjad Tower. Generated by build_letters.py from the abjad series and the fourteen muqaṭṭaʿāt. Mass is log10(abjad value) scaled — the ORDER is the source's, the compression is ours, and it is the only place the game bends the correspondence for playability. `form` records what the written glyph observably is; `registers` the three levels of the letter. Run with --verify to check against portal/db/turka.db.",
  "source_entries": [
    "ilm-al-huruf",
    "abjad-numerology"
  ],
  "mass_rule": "1.0 + 2.2 * log10(abjad), so alif=1.0 and ghayn=7.6",
  "form_note": "Observable facts about the standard isolated naskh form — orientation, dots and their position, whether the form encloses a counter, whether it descends below the line. Not doctrine.",
